actual_test_4_academic_listening_test_1_3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3125996-recent_actual_test_4_academic_listening_test_1_4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p><b>Penguins in Africa</b></p><p><b>Appearance and lifestyle</b></p><p>They are also called Jackass Penguins for the sound they make.</p><p>The <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of their body remains constant.</p><p>They restrict their <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> on land from dusk till dawn.</p><p>They cannot fly because they have heavy <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</p><p>They nest under the tree <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</p><p>They eat tree <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</p><p><b>Predators</b></p><ul><li>seals</li><li><span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>seagulls (eat the penguin <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> )</li></ul><p><b>Threats</b></p><p>They lose <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in winter.</p><p>They are fighting for nesting <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and food because of human activities.</p><p>In order to improve survivorship, it is helpful to increase the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of their genes.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_4_academic_listening_test_1_4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-q1","part_id":"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-practice-source-4-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","question_text":"",